# A guest throws a rock at glass, and the host removes the rock while it flies. What she sent of
# the flight before she heard (its states, its release and its claim of the glass) names a body the
# host no longer has: stale, dropped. The glass stands, and the rock is gone everywhere.
scenario remove_owned
scene glass_door
seed 7
guests 1
settle 6s

net g1 rtt 100ms jitter 20ms loss 2% reorder 10% reorder_delay 40ms

p1 grab rock_a as lift
at 1s p1 throw glass speed 7 as throw
# A removal two ticks after the rock meets the glass on the thrower's world reaches her after her
# contact, and her claim and release of it reach the host after the removal (recall_flight).
p0 remove rock_a on p1 contact glass +2t as remove

expect result lift granted
expect result throw done
expect result remove done
# The late claim existed and named a body the host had removed: stale, nothing came of it.
expect claims.count >= 1
expect claims_rejected.count >= 1
expect claim_effects.count <= 0
expect moved glass <= 1cm
expect late_drops.count >= 1
# What she sent of the rock under her old number until she heard: about a state a tick over the
# move's trip to her, a lost record's resend and her release.
expect late_drops.count <= 30
# Gone everywhere: a body only a guest still had would fail the agreement.
expect agree_at_rest 5cm 5deg
expect no_stuck
expect effects_once
